TRANSLATION QUALITY RULES:

🎯 LEVEL MATCHING:
- Translated text MUST maintain the SAME CEFR level as English source
- If English uses simple present, Turkish should use equivalent simplicity
- Vocabulary complexity must match between languages

📏 TURKISH LANGUAGE ADJUSTMENTS:
- Turkish sentences can be 10-15% longer than English (agglutinative nature)
- This is acceptable and natural, do not force shorter sentences

{{#if (eq level "A1")}}
TÜRKÇE A1 KURALLARI:
- Basit çekimler: -yor, -di, -ir/ar
- Kısa ekler, zincirleme ek kullanma (örn: "yapmaktaydılar" yerine "yapıyorlardı")
- Türkçe kökenli kelimeleri tercih et (Arapça/Farsça origin kaçın)
- Her cümlede 1 fiil
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq level "A2")}}
TÜRKÇE A2 KURALLARI:
- Temel bağlaçlar: ve, ama, çünkü, sonra
- Basit zaman ekleri
- Yaygın Osmanlıca kelimeler kabul edilebilir
- Kısa yan cümleler
{{/if}}

🔄 CONSISTENCY:
- Terminology must be consistent throughout (same term = same translation)
- Proper nouns should remain unchanged or use established Turkish forms
- Technical terms should be explained in parentheses on first use

⚠️ AVOID:
- Word-for-word translation that sounds unnatural
- English sentence structure forced onto Turkish
- Overly formal register for lower CEFR levels